  "content": {
    "title": "Cincinnati police declare The Banks 'closed,' disperse crowd",
    "text": "Updated March 26, 2026, 11:13 p.m. ETAs Cincinnati police advanced upon a crowd deemed unruly at The Banks on March 26, 2026, several people fell over and dropped their belongings.David Ferrara/The EnquirerAs Cincinnati police advanced upon a crowd deemed unruly at The Banks on March 26, 2026, several people fell over and dropped their belongings.David Ferrara/The EnquirerCincinnati police declared The Banks closed just after 8:30 p.m. Thursday, March 26 as crowds gathered after Reds Opening Day in downtown Cincinnati.Aaron Valdez/The EnquirerDozens of Cincinnati police, armed with riot shields, nonlethal shotguns and pepper spray, split a crowd in half at The Banks and declared it \"closed for the night\" on Opening Day on March 26, 2026.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerPeople cross Theodore M. Berry Way after Cincinnati police declared it \"closed for the night\" on Opening Day on March 26, 2026.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerCincinnati police block Marian Spencer Way at The Banks after the entertainment district was declared closed for the night on Opening Day, March 26, 2026, following \"disorder and violence\" as large crowds gathered.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerThe Roebling Bridge was closed after Cincinnati police declared The Banks \"closed for the night\" on Opening Day on March 26, 2026. after 'disorder and violence' after large crowds gathered.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerDozens of Cincinnati police, armed with riot shields, nonlethal shotguns and pepper spray, split a crowd in half at The Banks and declared it \"closed for the night\" on Opening Day on March 26, 2026.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerTraffic is backed up on Second Street after Cincinnati police declared The Banks \"closed for the night\" on Opening Day on March 26, 2026 after \"disorder and violence'.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerCincinnati Reds fans navigate crime scene tape after police declared The Banks closed on Opening Day, March 26, 2026.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerCincinnati Police placed crime scene tape at The Banks after police shut down the entertainment district after 'disorder and violence'.Cara Owsley/ The EnquirerCincinnati police deployed SWAT, CDRT and several other units to The Banks for Opening Day on March 26, 2026.David Ferrara/The EnquirerCincinnati police declared The Banks closed just after 8:30 p.m. Thursday, March 26 as crowds gathered after Reds Opening Day in downtown Cincinnati.Aaron Valdez/The EnquirerDowntown police Captain David Schofield, back to camera, counted down to lines of bike officers and SWAT before they advanced to the crowd, counting \"3, 2, 1, GO\" as police split the crowd and declared the area closed for the night, Thursday, March 26, 2026.David Ferrara/The EnquirerInterim CPD Chief Adam Hennie, right, and Sgt. Anthony Mitchell speak to reporters at The Banks after police closed the area Thursday, March 25, 2026. A large crowd had gathered following the Reds Opening Day game.Cara Owsley/The EnquirerInterim Cincinnati Police Chief Adam Hennie standing at The Banks during a large police response on March 26, 2026.Quinlan Bentley/The EnquirerPeople are seen leaving The Banks after 9:30 p.m. Thursday, March 26, 2026, after Cincinnati police declared it closed for the night. Large crowds had gathered in the area after the Reds Opening Day game.Cara Owsley/The EnquirerPeople are seen around The Banks after 9:30 p.m. Thursday, March 26, 2026.Cincinnati police declared it closed for the night just after 8 p.m.. Large crowds had gathered in the area following the Reds Opening Day game.Cara Owsley/The EnquirerJada Denise talks to reporters during a large police response at The Banks on March 26, 2026.Quinlan Bentley/The EnquirerAn armored Cincinnati police SWAT vehicle at The Banks during a large police response on March 26, 2026.Quinlan Bentley/The EnquirerCincinnati police officers at The Banks during a large police response on March 26, 2026.Quinlan Bentley/The EnquirerCincinnati police at The Banks during a large police response on March 26, 2026.Quinlan Bentley/The EnquirerCincinnati police officers at The Banks during a large police response on March 26, 2026.Quinlan Bentley/The EnquirerCincinnati police officers lined up at The Banks during a large police response on March 26, 2026.Quinlan Bentley/The Enquirer",
